&#8220;This album is a love story, but love stories are never one-dimensional,&#8221; she told Daryl Hannah for the latest issue of Wonderland , which Cyrus guest edited. &#8220;They’re always layered.&#8221;

According to the publication, the star&#8217;s next full-length may come in a matter of months, possibly before the 2027 Grammys in February. &#8220;There is definitely a romantic thread weaving through it because, like all my records, it’s a reflection of where I am in my life,&#8221; Cyrus continued of the LP, noting it will have 10 tracks. &#8220;But this one feels especially meaningful because this feeling has stayed with me through multiple eras.&#8221;

&#8220;That’s something I hadn’t really experienced before,&#8221; she added. &#8220;A peaceful kind of love has become a theme across my last three records. Not just the love I share with someone else, but the love I’ve found for myself. That’s probably been the biggest evolution. Once your relationship with yourself changes, every relationship around you changes too. I think this record celebrates both of those equally.&#8221;

The former Disney star&#8217;s news comes on the heels of the announcement that she&#8217;d found a new label home Atlantic Records, which is owned by Warner Music Group, after 13 years with Sony. Her last album with prior label Columbia was Endless Summer Vacation , which reached No. 4 on the Billboard 200 and spawned the Grammy-winning, eight-week Billboard Hot 100 -topper &#8220;Flowers.&#8221;

&#8220;Usually I’m very certain of the destination, and sometimes that can almost obliterate the journey because I’m so focused on getting somewhere,&#8221; Cyrus said in the new interview. &#8220;This one was different. It was organic and really unforced. Something that was super helpful this time was I started with the tracklist and never veered from it. I knew it would be 10 songs. I roughly knew the sound and the concept. That gave me a really strong compass without making the process feel forced.&#8221;

